            <ArticleTitle>Dislodged stent: a simple retrieval technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>323-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a technique for retrieval of a dislodged coronary stent using a stiff angioplasty wire positioned beside the initial stent guidewire. This two-wire technique provides a better platform to move and position the snare device without moving the dislodged stent and thus lessens the risk of embolization. If a larger femoral sheath is needed for stent removal, this method facilitates sheath exchange. Cathet. Cardiovasc. Intervent. 47:323-324, 1999.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 1999 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
